# Analyze screenshots first

When the user attaches a screenshot, image, or says "see screenshot":

1. **Open the image file** from workspace assets or the attachment path — do not rely on conversation summaries or image descriptions alone.
2. **Describe what you see** that matters to the bug: layout, wrong text, missing UI, wrong colors, truncation, position, version string in title bar.
3. **Cross-check** screenshot claims against game logs and source — screenshot = what player sees; log = what code did.
4. **State explicitly** in the reply that the screenshot was opened and what it proves (one short paragraph, not a wall).

## Quest Tracker screenshot checklist

| Look for | Why |
|----------|-----|
| Title bar version (`Quest Tracker Reduxx [vX.Y.Z]`) | Installed build vs workspace `MOD_VERSION` |
| Window corner vs game UI | Default position/size for baked defaults |
| Text right margin vs tab row (`Hidden(0)` right edge) | Wrap-width bugs at 28pt font |
| `(step unknown)` vs real objective | Step resolver / wiki data gap |
| Blank list vs `(loading quest row…)` | Cache / nil helper regressions |
| Tab counts vs log `rebuild` line | List filter / category mismatch |

Never say "from your screenshot" without having read the image file in this session.
